WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.600
DIVORCE IN PEACE

2
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.240
You will not go in.
You have never been in there.

3
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.640
All will be divided equally.
What is going on in my half?

4
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.880
Half of this belongs to me.
I was the surety.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.720
My parents lent you the seed money.
Do you remember?

6
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.680
OK, OK. I’ll sell everything
and you can pay your share out.

7
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.880
Do you have to be so dramatic?
I could help in real on my half.

8
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.720
It doesn’t work like that.
It’s a concrete, integrated organism.

9
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.640
I would help to knead the dough.

10
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.240
To knead the dough?
You just want to meddle.

11
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.520
You want to complicate things
as much as possible.

12
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.440
No. I want to show you that…

13
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.440
for you to understand,
what you will actually lose.

14
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.640
What will I lose?
- Things you haven’t noticed.

15
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.240
When there’s nothing to notice,
there’s nothing to understand.

16
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.520
Just go away!
You’ll freak out the baker.

17
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.040
What baker you have there?
I want to see him.

18
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.560
Who is warming you by the stove?
Some rosy-cheeked baker boy?

19
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.520
Cosy and warm.
- Go and smooch your flute teacher!

20
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.760
It’s a shady business from the start.
What are you really baking in there?

21
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.520
I’m working here to earn money!

22
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.200
We are not finished with this yet!
- Go away!

23
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.440
We are not finished!
- Don’t come here! Go away!

24
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.880
Haven’t finished!

25
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.880
In divorce the key word is what?

26
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.640
Positivity.

27
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.160
It’s so easy to let the tiger out,
to roar and to accuse

28
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.640
and to turn this delicate topic
into something disgusting and ugly.

29
00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:23.240
And here comes the third
therapy mission – Memory Box.

30
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.000
You’ll share between you two
a nice story about your marriage,

31
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:37.800
which feels most lovely, beautiful,
bright, cute and positive. Right?

32
00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.680
Memory Box - open!

33
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.200
Well, that would be nice.

34
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.960
You’ll recall a nice story
and share it between yourself

35
00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.000
and try to be positive.

36
00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.680
Oh! But how would we…

37
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.360
You’ll sit down, burn incense.

38
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.400
Nice dimmed lights.

39
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.200
You’ll take a photo album

40
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:10.400
and recall the most lovely memory
about your marriage and share it.

41
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.280
Then store this delicate and lovely
moment by taking a nice photo

42
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.520
and mount it in the divorce diary.

43
00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.680
Divorce diary?

44
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:29.560
It’s a special diary.
If you wish you can buy it here.

45
00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:36.680
This one for 14.90
and with padlock for 19.90.

46
00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.800
I don’t know.
Should we have one with padlock?

47
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.480
Sorry!

48
00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.960
Excuse me, but these are my pyjamas.

49
00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:00.360
Now what? In my own house!
Bloody hell!

50
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.760
Aksel.

51
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.520
This Ave’s guy… that man…
He’s in there… right now.

52
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.720
He’s wearing my pyjamas.

53
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.880
Well, just be patient.
- What? Patient?

54
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.160
Look, lawyer sent some blank forms,
I printed out for you too.

55
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.880
Read through, have a look.
- What forms?

56
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.720
Divorce agreement.
We spoke about this. - What?

57
00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.440
Aksel, we spoke about this.
Divorce papers.

58
00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.080
I’ll have a guest this evening.

59
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.240
Try not to cut this house in two
before that.

60
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.120
A guest?
- A guest? Who?

61
00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.600
So read it through.
I have to go to work.

62
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.200
And don’t forget tonight’s
therapy mission, okay?

63
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.440
What was the key word?

64
00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.600
Well…
- Positivity.

65
00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.160
She is tightening the screws,
hammer and tongs.

66
00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:01.800
Turning up the heat all the time,
you can feel it physically.

67
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.800
An agreement… right… agreement.

68
00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.480
I have a feeling she is turning this
harsh and insensitive deliberately.

69
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.720
Lawyer’s agreement?
What does it mean?

70
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.560
She wants to go to court!
That what it means!

71
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.480
Get over it!
Law is my secret hobby.

72
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.320
We’ll chew this over,
all the way to the court.

73
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.880
She says lets sell all our property

74
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.840
and each will buy a new place
according to one’s wishes.

75
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:40.600
This is worst! Scorched earth policy.
Wells are poisoned, animals killed.

76
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.040
All is nicely put down in writing.

77
00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.320
When we get a divorce,
we wouldn’t live next door anymore.

78
00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.760
Is Laura really a wolf
in sheep’s clothing?

79
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.920
Tauno, I really don’t know.

80
00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.600
I even don’t know who Laura is.
What kind of life she lives?

81
00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:05.320
We have been together
for a quarter of a century.

82
00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.760
I have always been sure I know her,
could trust her.

83
00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.520
She was my kind of person.

84
00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:16.800
Turns out I don’t know her.
What kind of life she lives?

85
00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.320
Where she goes to? Who she is?
It’s my fault, isn’t it?

86
00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:27.640
You are not to be blamed.
You are a victim!

87
00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.600
Am I?
- You’re a victim.

88
00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.600
Right, I’m a victim.
- Just say it - “I am a victim”.

89
00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:40.520
I am a victim.
- I am a victim!

90
00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:44.520
Right! You are a victim.
- Of course I am a victim.

91
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:50.040
This bakery, who are working there?
- Exactly. Who?

92
00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.360
How do we know, who's working there?
- Don’t know. I don’t know.

93
00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.200
Have I ever visited this bakery?
- Have you? - No, I haven’t.

94
00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.600
How do we know with whom
she is there all day long?

95
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:00.920
I don’t know that.

96
00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:04.040
Some evil person
has her under his influence.

97
00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.320
Some impudent baker
wants to take my place.

98
00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.280
Some horny baker!

99
00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:15.480
A horny dough twister gauges at Laura,
hopes to get a good life.

100
00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.800
I am like an idiot
with my bloody violin.

101
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.440
Aksel, this place
must be taken under surveillance.

102
00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.400
Under surveillance!

103
00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:29.080
People take positive characteristic
somehow self-evidently.

104
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.000
Nobody talks about it.
Negativity is constantly on their lips.

105
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.800
Say something positive
about your partner.

106
00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:42.160
Right now. Let’s go.
Some positive qualities?

107
00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.440
Me?

108
00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.200
About Aksel?

109
00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.440
Mihkel!
- I’m going upstairs.

110
00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.200
Wait, Mihkel.

111
00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:41.080
We’ll have this positivity session
with mother. - Great!

112
00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.240
You will have a guest.
A girl from your course?

113
00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:52.360
Mona. I asked mother,
I know her name.

114
00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.400
Great!
- Mihkel!

115
00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.480
This… Right…

116
00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.320
Mihkel!

117
00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.480
Come here for a moment.

118
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.240
Have you noticed?
- What?

119
00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.720
About mother…
does she have somebody?

120
00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.800
I don’t know.

121
00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.320
Haven’t you… You were working
in the bakery in summer.

122
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.360
Did you notice anything?
- What?

123
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.960
Something going on with the baker?
With a colleague?

124
00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:36.920
There was nothing. We baked.

125
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:41.120
OK. Thank you.

126
00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.480
Thank you for cooperation.

127
00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.960
One, one. Panther has landed.

128
00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.080
Do you copy?

129
00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.520
Hello?

130
00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.680
Press the button when you speak.
Do you hear me?

131
00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.160
Yes. Hello?

132
00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:27.760
Yes, I hear you.
I’m on site, all is quiet.

133
00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.880
There’s no movement.
I’ll take up the position.

134
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.680
All right. Thanks!

135
00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.040
I’ll report right away
if something will happen.

136
00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.880
Understood, thanks!

137
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.840
Over and out.
- Thanks!

138
00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.240
Laura, you have to take care
of your nerves.

139
00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:57.720
In this the therapist is quite right,
Positivity, mental balance.

140
00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.520
You have to do that in quiet.

141
00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.960
It’s like a rebirth…
a soft birth experience.

142
00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.400
Yes, I do understand. Yes.

143
00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.720
And talk to your children.
They’ll need an explanation.

144
00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:16.880
They don’t demonstrate it,
but their feelings must be let out.

145
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.240
That’s mindful parenting for you.
Understand?

146
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.960
Listen, I can’t talk any longer,
I’m standing upside-down.

147
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.200
OK. Thank you, Mirjam.

148
00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:53.480
What are you doing there?
What's that noise? Jesus.

149
00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:59.120
The memories, positivity thing.
I’m making arrangements.

150
00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.800
Did you drop something?

151
00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:05.040
What? No, no, no. I’m…
Just arranging. It’s not ready yet.

152
00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:08.680
I’ll come down soon.
- I’ll call you soon. Right.

153
00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:12.320
Don’t set yourself on fire.
- What? No, I wouldn’t.

154
00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.560
Tauno, she came home.
One, one, one.

155
00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:24.640
She came home…
She arrived early, Tauno.

156
00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:34.440
I think I haven’t explained
this situation adequately.

157
00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:39.440
Maybe we owe you and Ave
more detailed explanation.

158
00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.280
I don’t know. That’s life.

159
00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.240
You have our blessing.

160
00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:49.640
Get a divorce if you want to.
You don’t have to worry about us.

161
00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:54.480
Me and Mona we can rent a flat
or a dorm room. Ave has her life.

162
00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.680
I can see this affects you
although you say nothing.

163
00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.760
But what can we do?
- Tell me, how do you feel?

164
00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.520
How do I feel?

165
00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.640
Well, when I was little,

166
00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:16.360
my friends’ parents divorced
and they argued and so on.

167
00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.160
Back then I was afraid
that you too will one day…

168
00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.880
Then the long Era of Silence arrived.

169
00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.360
I grew up and wasn’t afraid anymore.
As simple as that.

170
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:55.000
Oh hello! How are you?

171
00:13:55.120 --> 00:14:00.640
Wow! Are you serious?
- Yes, how are you?

172
00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:05.280
How does Ülo feel?
Has he settled in?

173
00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.440
Don’t worry, we will go to Spain
any day soon. - I see.

174
00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:12.960
Yes, we are fighting against
banning the bullfights.

175
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.360
What?

176
00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:19.360
For? Fight for banning
and against the bullfights.

177
00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.000
Things are already planned.

178
00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.800
We’ll shower us with fake blood…
All will get rough and tough!

179
00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.440
You and Ülo?

180
00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:29.960
Whole world’s activists will be there,
vegans, conservationists.

181
00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.920
This nonsense should be banned.
- Of course! That’s very good.

182
00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:37.200
Exactly. One most think global.
- When will you leave?

183
00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:42.640
Currently transport and route
are nailed down.

184
00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:48.280
Conservationists can’t fly, it pollutes.
Ships are also polluting.

185
00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.800
Some will take catamarans
and sailing boats across the ocean.

186
00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:59.000
Most low-impact would be swimming,
but… the ocean, you know.

187
00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:02.360
We’ll take an electric train
as far as we can.

188
00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:07.560
Then will hitchhike, but only on
electric cars. This will take time.

189
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.440
Blimey!

190
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.160
So we will be leaving soon.

191
00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:15.760
Listen, Ave, that’s really great
that you’ll care about all this.

192
00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:20.720
You wouldn’t understand anyway.
And mother doesn’t have an affair.

193
00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:21.800
What?

194
00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.880
Mihkel called me.
You’re unbelievable!

195
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.000
Positivity…

196
00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.920
Right.

197
00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:38.920
Beautiful memories.
Where should we start?

198
00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:44.320
When I was thinking about it,
all came down cascading.

199
00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:46.840
All the beautiful times we had.

200
00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:51.160
I can see that you are really trying.

201
00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.680
Aksel, this is really nice
that you are trying to divorce nicely.

202
00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.120
Well, I’m…

203
00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:01.360
What? Is this our camping trip?
- Yes, at Lake Peipus.

204
00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.640
Mirjam and Tauno.

205
00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.840
This was the time when Tauno stepped
into his own trap?

206
00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.640
He hung upside down from a pine tree.
We had to cut him down.

207
00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.560
My god, the end was quite nasty.
- Yes it was.

208
00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:23.440
Look, Ave’s first birthday.

209
00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.160
The cake.

210
00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:32.320
It was raining, I was walking
through the town in the rain.

211
00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.040
Even my underpants were soaking wet,
but cake was in one piece.

212
00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.920
I’ll remember.

213
00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.600
Look!

214
00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.440
Is this Mihkel?
- Birth of Mihkel.

215
00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:48.800
Dear god, he’s your spitting image.

216
00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.080
How young we were!
So happy!

217
00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:01.600
We’ve had so many happy moments.

218
00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:07.640
Must this all really end like this?
- Aksel, don’t start.

219
00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.640
Laura...

220
00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.160
Darling.

221
00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.280
This is swallow calling the duck.

222
00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:27.520
What is this?
- I don’t know. It’s my stomach.

223
00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.040
Should I bring you some water?
- That would be really nice.

224
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.480
There’s no movement.
I’m ending surveillance for tonight.

225
00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.120
Over and out.

226
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.800
Oh, thank you.
I feel better already.

227
00:17:56.920 --> 00:18:00.280
Jesus, we must care of ourselves.
This shouldn’t affect our health.

228
00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:06.440
Oh dear, I feel better already.
I feel much better.

229
00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.320
Allright.

230
00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.920
Thank you, Aksel.
This all was really nice.

231
00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:19.480
I have to check a few invoices.
Thanks. Very beautiful, positive.

232
00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.400
Bloody hell!

233
00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:29.840
Where did you throw it?
It’s an expensive gadget.

234
00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.520
Threw out of the window.

235
00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.160
It intruded brutally our nice,
intimate moment,

236
00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.120
which could have solved
our situation positively.

237
00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:42.680
So you’re hoping to work it out?
- Of course I’m hoping. Damn.

238
00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:46.680
Yes. I found it.
- Give it to me.

239
00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:53.520
Very good, tomorrow morning
I’ll go the bakery to keep watch.

240
00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:57.160
Let’s wait and see.
- Is this stalking worthwhile?

241
00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.480
Stop it! We all want to know
what is going on?

242
00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.920
I’ve been thinking,
maybe it’s about me.

243
00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.240
About you?

244
00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:10.480
Maybe I didn’t pay enough attention.
Wasn’t a nice and sensitive man.

245
00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:16.440
You are super! Super husband.
You both are super!

246
00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:20.880
Somebody has an evil hand in it.
To ruin your marital bliss.

247
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:26.000
Some mean playboy cake master!

248
00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.880
It’s completely crazy!
- You’ll upload it?

249
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:42.800
First episode is already uploaded.
10 minutes of “Divorce in Peace”.

250
00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:44.920
I also subtitled the video.

251
00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:49.280
How many viewers?
- Well, some.

252
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.600
Examining commission
is not interested in viewers.

253
00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:58.680
True, but something must be done.

254
00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.560
Are they really getting a divorce?

255
00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.880
It’s all pretty lame.

256
00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.080
Excuse me.

257
00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:38.000
She drove away.
- I can see. I’m already on move.

258
00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:41.280
When a stone blocks the way,
you’ll go around.

259
00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.280
Creek finds a river
even if this takes 100 years.

260
00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:52.080
I can see he’s trying in his own way,
the stone is trying to roll a little.

261
00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.840
Very good. Watch, breathe, live.

262
00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:59.640
If something will change, trust
will return, you can change your mind.

263
00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:01.120
Trust!

264
00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.000
I’ve missed it.

265
00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.840
Well, chicklings, little birds.

266
00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.160
All right, Mirjam. Thanks!
Let’s do that.

267
00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:21.400
Ants, what’s the matter?

268
00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:25.760
Well, the first bird.

269
00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.640
Georg has gone missing.
- Georg?

270
00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.880
Oh my God!

271
00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:40.760
Cage door was open,
hay and food untouched.

272
00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:45.880
Balcony window was open.
No sight of him at home and…

273
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.720
He will come back.
He has had adventures before.

274
00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:57.080
What if he doesn’t?
- Dear God!

275
00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.120
Bingo! Bloody hell!

276
00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:14.440
Aksel, do you hear me?
Double-crosser has been exposed.

277
00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:28.120
You’re here. Very good.

278
00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:34.960
Watch this. Scroll on from here.

279
00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:44.600
Sorry! Now it’s clear.

280
00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:48.200
It’s the baker, baker boy.

281
00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:53.880
Damn! I’ve seen him somewhere.

282
00:22:58.240 --> 00:23:01.000
Hell! He once brought Laura home.

283
00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:05.520
It could have been a lie!

284
00:23:05.640 --> 00:23:10.040
An excuse! A lie, an elaborate lie!
Bloody hell!

285
00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:13.520
Don’t worry!
I will squeeze him.

286
00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:14.960
How?

287
00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.560
I have my interrogation technique.
Hundred percent sure thing.

288
00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:20.800
Tested in Iraq and Afghanistan.

289
00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.640
Bloody hell!

290
00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:29.880
Here we go!

291
00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:34.440
Stop! Stop!
- What?

292
00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:40.440
Are you in hurry to get away?
- Excuse me?

293
00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:45.240
Name?
- I… do I have to tell you?

294
00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:47.920
Name?
- Ants. - Ants.

295
00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:52.240
Does Laura’s name ring a bell?

296
00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:57.440
Laura? What a question?
She is the owner of this bakery.

297
00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:59.640
What is your relationship with her?

298
00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:04.640
With Laura? I’m a baker here.
Working relationship.

299
00:24:04.760 --> 00:24:06.800
Affair at work!

300
00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:12.160
Confess willingly before
I’ll twist your arms. What is going on?

301
00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:17.520
Excuse me?
Sorry, but I really have to…

302
00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:20.880
Excuse me, what is going on?

303
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:25.800
I want to know too what is going on!
Are you taking me for a fool?

304
00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:29.760
First you want to pocket the bakery.

305
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:34.360
Hell, you ruin their marriage
and then pocket Laura’s bakery.

306
00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:37.880
Listen, I really have to…
- Bloody hell, horny baker!

307
00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.680
Other people’s marital bliss
means nothing to you?

308
00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.520
What? Hell, really...

309
00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:46.120
Are we going to talk?

310
00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:49.840
Tauno, that’s enough.
What are you doing!

311
00:24:58.680 --> 00:25:02.520
Aksel!
- I’m sorry, he…

312
00:25:02.640 --> 00:25:05.720
Ants, what is going on?
Are you all right?

313
00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:11.760
Something positive about Aksel?

314
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:23.120
Aksel is sometimes impetuous,
but good-hearted.

315
00:25:25.160 --> 00:25:31.280
He wouldn’t hurt a fly.
Because he likes to take it easy.

316
00:25:34.160 --> 00:25:36.440
Thanks!

317
00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:42.280
I’m not a murderer
only because I’m too lazy.

318
00:25:42.400 --> 00:25:44.040
Thank you!

319
00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:47.400
Ants!

320
00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:49.760
Go away!

321
00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:52.440
What are you doing?
You come here to threaten Ants?

322
00:25:52.560 --> 00:25:53.680
I’m sorry, but he…

323
00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:56.360
He has enough problems
and you come here like this,

324
00:25:56.480 --> 00:26:01.320
disgustingly, violently, brutally.
Disgusting, this is disgusting.

325
00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:02.600
Laura!

326
00:26:02.720 --> 00:26:06.800
Ants, go home. Take some days off.
Take tomorrow off too.

327
00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:10.880
I’m really sorry for all this.
I’m really embarrassed.

328
00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:15.320
I wanted to be sure…

329
00:26:15.440 --> 00:26:19.840
You cheated on me
and now you dear to spy on me!

330
00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:22.680
And so wrongly! So disgustingly!

331
00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:24.520
I wanted to know,
why do you want a divorce.

332
00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:26.560
I have already told you.

333
00:26:26.680 --> 00:26:30.000
This is another reason
if you had any kind of doubt.

334
00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:34.720
Hell, I already thought that…
Enough. Enough!

335
00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:55.520
Excuse me.

336
00:26:55.640 --> 00:27:00.640
Sorry! It’s not about you,
it’s about me again.

337
00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:02.440
Please forgive me.

338
00:27:05.440 --> 00:27:08.440
Tell me, am I a bad person?
Roberta, tell me honestly.

339
00:27:08.560 --> 00:27:10.960
No. No!

340
00:27:12.920 --> 00:27:18.520
I don’t know. I don’t feel good.
I feel like I deserve to be punished.

341
00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:24.120
Maybe we should have
a longer lesson again on Wednesday?

342
00:27:31.200 --> 00:27:33.520
Oh, this is mine.

343
00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:41.120
You are the best!
- Thank you.

344
00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:52.080
What?

345
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:03.400
Mona!

346
00:28:04.440 --> 00:28:07.960
Can you imagine!
Video has over 20 thousand viewers.

347
00:28:10.520 --> 00:28:12.440
Hello, Laura.
- Hello.

348
00:28:17.120 --> 00:28:18.960
So...

349
00:28:19.640 --> 00:28:23.120
So, we’ll carry on?
- It seems so. Yes, it seems so.

350
00:28:28.680 --> 00:28:30.880
That’s what!

351
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.960
Our mystical Mister X...

352
00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:38.680
The horny baker,
he was just a cover.

353
00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.880
This man is a total stranger.

354
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.640
Stranger? This is Rihard Engel,
restaurant chain owner.

355
00:28:46.760 --> 00:28:48.600
A multimillionaire!
